The Syntax and Group of Predeterminated Git Features for .ksh files:

git.branch();
--------------

Shows the branch in were we are stading right now at
our code, for efficiency and understanding. This funcion
be refresh in every single command, like all the rest of
this syntax code.

git.repo();
------------

This one feature show us the repository in which
we are working for, using this type of definition for
not to be noisy "RepoCreator/RepositoryName", simple
but efficient.

git.commitsDous();
-------------------

One of the most important and useful features
bring the ability of known how much commits
we have done in the current branch.

A lot of more GIT FEATURES will be created in the future, enjoy!
